.TH SDL_CreateAudioStream 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateAudioStream \- Create a new audio stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AudioStream * SDL_CreateAudioStream(const SDL_AudioSpec *src_spec, const SDL_AudioSpec *dst_spec);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that
.BR src_spec
or
.BR dst_spec
may be NULL, but any attempts to put or get data from an audio stream will fail until it has valid specs assigned to both ends of the stream\[char46] Specs can be assigned later through
.BR SDL_SetAudioStreamFormat (),
or binding the stream to an audio device (which will set the format of only the input or output, depending on what kind of device the stream was bound to)\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I src_spec
the format details of the input audio\[char46] May be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I dst_spec
the format details of the output audio\[char46] May be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a new audio stream on success or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

